<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jerónimos Monastery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jerónimos Monastery is a monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> built from the early sixteenth century in the ornate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manueline-style">Manueline style</a>. Its construction was funded by revenues from the spice trade. It is a symbol of the wealth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> in the age of discovery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeronimos-monastery.jpg" alt="Jerónimos Monastery" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Holger Uwe Schmitt · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1502_legte_K%C3%B6nig_Manuel_I._den_Grundstein_f%C3%BCr_das_Hieronymus_Kloster_in_Lissabon._06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
